/-
As an immediate consequence of Theorem \ref{thm:mainisoperim} [1.1] we settle a conjecture of Kahn
and Park \cite[Conjecture 1.3]{KP20} on cube partitions:
-/

/-- **Theorem 1.2** ([DIRX]). Let $(A,B,W)$ be a partition of $\{0,1\}^n$ and assume
$|A|=\frac12$. Then
$$|\nabla(A,B)|+\sqrt n\,|W|\ge\tfrac12.$$
Here $|W|=\mathbf{E}\mathbf{1}_W$ and
$|\nabla(A,B)|=2^{-n}\#\{(x,y)\in\mathcal{E} : x\in A,y\in B\}$, where $\mathcal{E}$ is the set of
edges of $\{0,1\}^n$. -/
theorem thm_1_2 (n : ℕ) (hn : 1 ≤ n) (A B W : Set ({0,1}^n))
    (hAB : Disjoint A B) (hAW : Disjoint A W) (hBW : Disjoint B W)
    (hcover : A ∪ B ∪ W = Set.univ) (hA : ｜A｜ = 1 / 2) :
    |∇(A, B)| + √n * ｜W｜ ≥ 1 / 2 := by
  sorry

/-- [DIRX], §1, Theorem 1.2: this settles the conjecture of Kahn and Park [KP20, Conjecture 1.3]
(formalized in [DIR] as `Auto.DIR.KahnParkConjecture`, with $n^{0.5}$ in place of $\sqrt n$). -/
theorem kahnParkConjecture : KahnParkConjecture := by
  sorry

/-
